+## Native ACP harness
+
+On a build with bqAgent support, the following `orca-plugin.json` can be the only file in a plugin directory:
+
+```json
+{
+  "manifestVersion": 2,
+  "id": "bqagent",
+  "name": "bqAgent",
+  "version": "1.0.0",
+  "engines": { "orca": ">=1.4.248" },
+  "execution": "declarative",
+  "capabilities": [{ "kind": "agent:launch" }],
+  "contributes": {
+    "agentHarnesses": [{ "id": "bqagent", "command": "bqagent", "args": ["--acp"] }]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Run `orca plugin install <directory>` and review the requested grant before approving its fingerprint. The host needs a separately installed `bqagent` executable.
+
